[gd_scene load_steps=8 format=3 uid="uid://endcap0sfgdmvp"]

; SHELF-1 (2026-09-19) — AN END-CAP: the short display that closes the end of an aisle and faces
; the cross-aisle. ShelfUnit.tscn's construction exactly, 1.40 m long instead of 2.30 — read that
; file's header for the shelf heights, the missing back panel and the grey, all of which are the
; same here and are deliberately not restated so the two cannot drift.
;
; 1.40 m long (x) x 1.80 m tall (y) x 0.50 m deep (z), origin at the FLOOR, centred.
;
; IT IS INSTANCED ROTATED 90 deg ABOUT Y in SearchRoom.tscn, so its length runs along the room's
; z and its 0.50 m depth faces the cross-aisle. The bay is symmetric about both horizontal axes
; (uprights at +/-0.67, boards centred), so +90 and -90 occupy the IDENTICAL volume — which is
; the one reason the basis-row trap in .claude/rules/godot-scenes.md cannot bite here. It still
; got a headed look; see docs/qa/2026-09-19-shelf-1/.
;
; LEVEL geometry, no script, listed in SupermarketWorldSelfTest.SectionScenes for the reason
; ShelfUnit.tscn's header gives.

